">Qualified as:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Premier League champions &middot; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Man City</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&mdash; FA Cup winners</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="font-weight:700">Missing:</span><span>&nbsp;</span><span style="font-weight:700">Saliba</span><span>&nbsp;(back), </span><span style="font-weight:700">Timber</span><span>&nbsp;(groin surgery), </span><span style="font-weight:700">Copley</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(ACL)</span></p><h3 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:14pt;padding-bottom:12pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:14pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The Road In &mdash; Arsenal&#39;s Pre-Season</span></h3><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Aug 1</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Girona</span><span>&nbsp;1-4 </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Havertz</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tzolis</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Dowman</span><span>, </span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Jesus</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Aug 5</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;1-3 </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Real Betis</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Dublin; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Hincapi&eacute;</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;scored</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Aug 9</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;2-3 </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Borussia Dortmund</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; Emirates Cup; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nwaneri</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gy&ouml;keres</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;(pen); shootout won 5-4</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Aug 12</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;v </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Como</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&mdash; Emirates, 7:30pm BST; kicking off as this edition goes out</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">Six conceded in the two defeats. Two clean sheets in four pre-season matches: none.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The vacancy on the left that nobody has filled</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Vinicius Junior re-signed at Madrid. Morgan Rogers went to Chelsea. Galatasaray have bid &euro;40m for Gabriel Martinelli and been told no &mdash; because Arsenal cannot sell a left winger they have not yet replaced.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The single defining failure of </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s summer, if it ends as it currently stands, will be the left wing. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Andrea Berta</span><span>&nbsp;spent the window chasing an elite left-sided forward and has so far come away with </span><span style="font-weight:700">Tzolis</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;&mdash; a very good signing at &pound;34m, and not the signing the club set out to make.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>The headline pursuit was </span><span style="font-weight:700">Vinicius J&uacute;nior</span><span>. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;monitored his contract situation closely as he entered the final year of his deal at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Real Madrid</span><span>; Sky Sports News had reported for more than a week that he would stay, and on August 6 he signed a six-year extension through 2032. Those close to the player always expected as much, and there is a reasonable reading in which </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s interest served chiefly to improve his terms. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Morgan Rogers</span><span>&nbsp;went to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Chelsea</span><span>&nbsp;for a reported &pound;117m. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bradley Barcola</span><span>&nbsp;is available in principle from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Paris Saint-Germain</span><span>&nbsp;but at a valuation reported at &euro;150m, with </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Liverpool</span><span>&nbsp;also in the conversation. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nico Williams</span><span>&nbsp;has a release clause at </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Athletic Club</span><span>&nbsp;of roughly &pound;77m and, per TEAMtalk, Berta has held discussions to assess whether it is doable. The Independent has named </span><span style="font-weight:700">Juli&aacute;n &Aacute;lvarez</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Iliman Ndiaye</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;on the same shortlist. Nothing has moved to a bid.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span>Into that vacuum has walked </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Galatasaray</span><span>, who submitted a &euro;40m (&pound;34m) offer for </span><span style="font-weight:700">Gabriel Martinelli</span><span>&nbsp;&mdash; first flagged as an exploratory approach by </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ben Jacobs</span><span>, then reported as a formal bid by The Sun. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;rejected it on valuation, believing the 25-year-old is worth more in the current market, and the club has been unambiguous with anyone who asks: </span><span style="font-weight:700">Martinelli</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;does not leave until a replacement arrives. He is said to be open to the move. He scored once in 30 Premier League appearances last season, 11 goals and seven assists across all 52. He is also, right now, the only senior left-sided forward at the club with Premier League title medals and a functioning relationship with the way Arteta wants that flank to work.</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>The arithmetic is uncomfortable and it is also historic. </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s record sale remains </span><span style="font-weight:700">Alex Oxlade-Chamberlain</span><span>&#39;s &pound;35m move to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Liverpool</span><span>&nbsp;in August 2017 &mdash; nine years of market inflation and not one player sold above it. </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Galatasaray</span><span>&#39;s &pound;34m sits just under that line, which is part of why it was refused; reported valuations of </span><span style="font-weight:700">Martinelli</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;in the &pound;45m-&pound;50m range would break the record outright, and the Mirror framed Wednesday&#39;s developments in exactly those terms. Selling well is exactly what a well-run club does. Selling in the wrong order, with &pound;144m already committed in fees this summer and no replacement secured, is how a champion arrives at September 2 light in its weakest area. The window closes at 11pm on Tuesday, September 1.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">TRANSFER NEWS</span></h2><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&pound;75m for Bruno: Arsenal buy a captain, and Newcastle lose one</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">Confirmed, August 8. Four-year deal, squad number 39, and a Brazilian who started all five of his country&#39;s World Cup matches. Newcastle did not want to sell.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;completed the signing of </span><span style="font-weight:700">Bruno Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>&nbsp;from </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle United</span><span>&nbsp;on August 8 for &pound;75m, with around &pound;7m of that figure due to </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Olympique Lyonnais</span><span>&nbsp;under a sell-on clause. The 28-year-old has signed a four-year contract and will wear 39. It is the second-largest fee in </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&#39;s history and the clearest statement of intent the club has made since winning the title.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>&nbsp;leaves </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle</span><span>&nbsp;after four and a half years, 195 appearances, 31 goals and 32 assists, having captained the club to the 2025 League Cup &mdash; their first domestic trophy in seventy years. The Daily Mail reported this week that </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Newcastle</span><span>&nbsp;did not want to sell and that a &quot;very emotional&quot; </span><span style="font-weight:700">Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>&nbsp;asked to leave. He arrives in form: he started all five of </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Brazil</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&#39;s matches at this summer&#39;s World Cup and registered four assists.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="font-weight:700">Andrea Berta</span><span>, the sporting director, framed it as a leadership signing as much as a footballing one: &quot;Bruno is a player with a great mentality and quality, who will bring strong leadership to our squad,&quot; he said, noting the depth it creates alongside </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rice</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Zubimendi</span><span>. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Guimar&atilde;es</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">&nbsp;himself was blunter. &quot;I need a challenge like this,&quot; he said. &quot;I want to win trophies, I want to make history.&quot;</span></p><p style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;padding-left:0;font-size:11pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span>The tactical consequence is a genuine selection headache and a squeeze further down. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Rice</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Zubimendi</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Guimar&atilde;es</span><span>, </span><span style="font-weight:700">Mikel Merino</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="font-weight:700">&Oslash;degaard</span><span>&nbsp;cannot all play. </span><span style="font-weight:700">Myles Lewis-Skelly</span><span>, 19, who featured in the Champions League semi-final against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Atl&eacute;tico Madrid</span><span>&nbsp;and in the final against </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">PSG</span><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">, is the player most obviously affected &mdash; see The Rumour Mill below.</span></p><h2 style="padding-top:0pt;margin:0;color:#000000;font-weight:700;padding-left:0;font-size:18pt;padding-bottom:11.2pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left;padding-right:0"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:18pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:normal">The centre-back hunt: Konsa reignited, Romero a non-starter, Stones free</span></h2><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#000000;font-weight:400;text-decoration:none;vertical-align:baseline;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;font-style:italic">With Saliba&#39;s back injury open-ended and Timber weeks away, Arsenal have returned to Aston Villa for Ezri Konsa. The gap is money, and it is wide.</span></p><p style="padding:0;margin:0;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;;line-height:1.0;text-align:left"><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&nbsp;have reignited their interest in </span><span style="font-weight:700">Ezri Konsa</span><span>, the 28-year-old </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Aston Villa</span><span>&nbsp;and </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">England</span><span>&nbsp;defender, with the BBC and the Mirror both reporting movement on Wednesday and </span><span style="font-weight:700">Nicol&ograve; Schira</span><span>&nbsp;independently confirming the interest. The picture from the various reports is consistent on the shape and inconsistent on the numbers: </span><span style="color:#ef0107;font-weight:700">Arsenal</span><span>&#39;s opening offer was rebuffed, </span><span style="color:#023474;font-weight:700">Villa</span><span>&nbsp;value </span><span style="font-